     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Comment from Sourceforge Task&#93;</span><br/>\nComment Submitter: cwilper<br/>\nSCOPE REDUCTION:<br/>\nThis task does not require content model validation as part of the error description.  A follow-on task (see original feature request for reference) will do this.</p>\n\n<p>REVIEW NOTES:<br/>\nI verified the following behavior when manually testing this branch:</p>\n\n<p>a) When BMech is missing, the dissemination fails with a 404 and a note indicating which BMech is missing.<br/>\nb) When CModel is missing, the dissemination fails with a 404 and a note indicating which CModel is missing.<br/>\nc) When a bound datastream is missing, the dissemination fails with a 500 and a n unfriendly stack trace<span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span>.</p>\n\n<p>Case (c) still needs to be handled (it should respond with a 404 and a message indicating which datastream(s) were missing) before closing this task out.</p>\n\n<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;1&#93;</span> fedora.server.errors.GeneralException: Error getting <br/>\n\tat fedora.server.access.dissemination.DisseminationService.get(DisseminationService.java:961)<br/>\n\tat fedora.server.access.dissemination.DisseminationService.getDisseminationContent(DisseminationService.java:991)<br/>\n\tat fedora.server.access.dissemination.DisseminationService.assembleDissemination(DisseminationService.java:637)<br/>\n\tat fedora.server.access.DefaultAccess.getDissemination(DefaultAccess.java:419)<br/>\n\tat fedora.server.access.FedoraAccessServlet.getDissemination(FedoraAccessServlet.java:707)<br/>\n\tat fedora.server.access.FedoraAccessServlet.doGet(FedoraAccessServlet.java:449)</p>",
